For chaotic monks:
#1 would not be helpful, as they often do not *have* a weapon.  Ditto 
(partially) #3.

#4 could be irritating:
*Clang*
"A blessed +1 longsword?  I can see how much effort you put into this 
choice of gift.  I mean, you could have given me a ring of conflict or 
speed/jumping boots, but no, you though that the perfect gift for a 
martial arts expert was a longsword."
Maybe change it to a spellbook too.

#5 would not be too useful either, unless it boosts you beyond 
speed-boots levels.  (Eat my dust, air-elementals!)  How about intrinsic 
bullet-time instead?  We need some Matrix references.  :-P

The change to the crowning gift is very good though, as monks will have 
many of the intrinsics already.

